  "Il faut diviser par ‖{nm}‖² = ⟨{nm}, {nm}⟩.": "You must divide by ‖{nm}‖² = ⟨{nm}, {nm}⟩.",
  "Coefficient de {nm} : ⟨q, {nm}⟩ / ⟨{nm}, {nm}⟩": "Coefficient of {nm}: ⟨q, {nm}⟩ / ⟨{nm}, {nm}⟩",
  "Valeurs aux points": "Values at the points",
  "Vérifier que ⟨1, t⟩ = 0": "Check that ⟨1, t⟩ = 0",
  "Projeter directement sur 1 et t": "Project directly onto 1 and t",
  "La formule de projection demande une base orthogonale : vérifie d'abord ⟨1, t⟩ = 0.": "The projection formula needs an orthogonal basis: first check ⟨1, t⟩ = 0.",
  "⟨1, t⟩ : la base (1, t) est-elle orthogonale ?": "⟨1, t⟩: is the basis (1, t) orthogonal?",
  "Base orthogonale": "Orthogonal basis",
  "La projection est un polynôme : c₀·1 + c₁·t.": "The projection is a polynomial: c₀·1 + c₁·t.",
  "La projection c₀·1 + c₁·t": "The projection c₀·1 + c₁·t",
  "Sur P₂, on pose ⟨p, q⟩ = {def}. Projette q = {q} sur Span{1, t}.": "On P₂, define ⟨p, q⟩ = {def}. Project q = {q} onto Span{1, t}.",
  "Vérifie que 1 et t sont orthogonaux pour ce produit, puis applique la formule de projection avec ⟨ , ⟩.": "Check that 1 and t are orthogonal for this inner product, then apply the projection formula with ⟨ , ⟩.",
  "⟨t, 1⟩ (et ⟨1, 1⟩ = 3)": "⟨t, 1⟩ (and ⟨1, 1⟩ = 3)",
